<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrius Zvonimir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1089</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Dmitar Zvonimir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demetrius Zvonimir was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> from 1076 to 1089, having earlier been ban of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a>. He was crowned at Solin in 1076 by a legate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a>, swearing loyalty to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. His death without an heir led to a succession struggle in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-i-of-hungary">Ladislaus I of Hungary</a>, brother of his wife Helen, intervened, ending in the union of Croatia with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1102.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demetrius-zvonimir.jpg" alt="Demetrius Zvonimir" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samuel Wein · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SplitBaptistryKing.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
